Sascha,

When you compile stuff with gcc, you can tell it to use specific libraries.
To do this you supply a command line argument such as "-lm" (this says, use
the maths library). -lX11 is telling gcc to use the X11 library. But it
seems your gcc cannot find it.

I know it's not much help, but it's an explanation as to what is going
wrong. Stick around and someone else here may be able to give you a better
answer such as where the libraries should be, or what to look for in the
source distribution for X11 that may be making this fail.

Cheers,

Collin

